We are using this as a payload wrapper for JAXRS services. The payload can be any type at runtime. Unless we set the extraClass, the JAXBContext created in AbstractJAXBProvider is not picking up the actual parameter types. I was thinking of extending to add to existing jaxb context map, i could not since its a private scoped hashmap. This should be automatically handled in AbstractJAXBProvider class. Following check can be made and added for actual type. 

ParameterizedType paramType = (genericType instanceof ParameterizedType) ? (ParameterizedType) genericType: null; 
if (paramType.getActualTypeArguments().length > 0) { 
// Fetch the actual type at index 0 
